Azure infrastructure occasionally requires planned maintenance to maintain platform reliability, security, and performance. Organizations should understand how planned maintenance can affect workloads and prepare appropriate operational responses.

Maintenance planning may involve:

* Reviewing Service Health information
* Identifying affected resources
* Checking workload redundancy
* Scheduling application maintenance
* Communicating with stakeholders
* Validating recovery procedures

For example, an enterprise running redundant application instances can continue serving users even when infrastructure maintenance affects individual resources.

A real-life use case is a banking organization preparing operations teams for scheduled cloud maintenance without disrupting customer services.

Understanding planned maintenance helps organizations distinguish expected platform activity from unexpected outages.
